# Where `ship.sh` and `registry.sh` send things — copy to deploy/target.env and edit.
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT FLAGS. Every ship took `REMOTE=… PORT=… FAST=…` in front of it. A run that
# forgot one went to the wrong machine, or died on a refused connection after it had already built,
# pushed and PINNED — leaving a values file naming a digest the cluster does not run.
#
# NOT IN GIT: it names a host and a login, and those differ per operator and per environment.

# The pilot, reached directly (put the key in ~/.ssh/config for this host):
# REMOTE=root@8.213.51.70
# PORT=22

# A local VM reached through a forwarded port — the older default:
# REMOTE=tamam@127.0.0.1
# PORT=2224

# `1` pushes layers through the registry (deploy/registry.sh), `0` sends the whole image over ssh.
# FAST=0

# ── Meta, for the console bundle (see deploy/publish-images.sh) ────────────────────────────────
#
# BAKED IN AT BUILD, NOT SET ON THE POD. Vite inlines these into the JavaScript, so an image built
# without them cannot be configured afterwards — and «اربط واتساب» then says «الربط غير مُفعَّل
# بعد», which is honest and useless. Leave them out until the application exists; fill them and
# rebuild the console image on the day it does.
#
# VITE_META_APP_ID=
# VITE_META_CONFIG_ID=

# The Graph version FB.init is pinned to. Meta retires versions on a schedule, so this names the
# one we tested against rather than drifting to whatever the SDK defaults to.
# It is also the version the ONBOARDING adapter speaks (see notification-service values): the
# console once pinned v21.0 while that adapter called v26.0, which is one product holding two
# conversations with Meta. `ci/check_the_meta_versions_are_alive.py` refuses a second answer.
# VITE_META_GRAPH_VERSION=v26.0

# THERE IS NO EMBEDDED SIGNUP VERSION SETTING, and there cannot be one. Meta retires v2 and v3 on
# 15 October 2026; v4 takes no parameters and reads its version from the Facebook Login for
# Business CONFIGURATION behind VITE_META_CONFIG_ID. Choosing it is a change on Meta's side.

# ── Moyasar, for the card form (see apps/console/src/payment.ts) ───────────────────────────────
#
# SAME SHAPE AS META'S THREE ABOVE — baked in at build, absent means the card form correctly
# declares itself unavailable (`canMintToken`) instead of pretending to work. This is the
# PUBLISHABLE key only — safe to ship in client code, it can create a single-use card token and
# nothing else. The secret key stays server-side, in billing-service's own credentials, never here.
# VITE_MOYASAR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
